CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ destructor body completes: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ one uncaught exception: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ inner exception caught: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ outer exception caught: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ none after the handler: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A destructor called during stack unwinding saw the unwound exception as
in flight after each call in its body and left it early.  The exception
lowering now saves and clears the in-flight exception around such a call
and counts the exception for std::uncaught_exceptions.
